{%- comment -%}
  A nav item that scrolls to a section of the home page.

  Rendered only by header-drawer, and hidden above the phone breakpoint by
  .hp-nav-jump — these are shortcuts for a small screen, where the sections in
  question are a long scroll down, not for a desktop nav that is already short.

  The href is a real URL to the home page plus the anchor, so it works before
  JavaScript runs and from any other page in the store. When the target is on
  the current page, hp-theme.js intercepts the click to close the drawer and
  scroll with the sticky header's height taken off.

  Accepts:
    label       {string} link text; nothing renders when blank
    anchor      {string} the target element's id, e.g. hp-colours
    item_class  {string} the host menu's own item class
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if label != blank and anchor != blank -%}
  <li class="hp-nav-jump">
    <a
      href="{{ routes.root_url }}#{{ anchor }}"
      class="{{ item_class }}"
      data-hp-jump="{{ anchor }}"
    >
      <span>{{ label | escape }}</span>
    </a>
  </li>
{%- endif -%}
